      "stageRecord": "The sentence coordinates two independent propositions: Mia reads the book, and Leo writes a letter. In this GB analysis, German VP and IP are underlyingly head-final, while the surface declaratives will be verb-second CPs. Each subject is generated in Spec-IP, the traditional GB external-argument position adopted here; no VP-internal subject movement is assumed. Each accusative object is the complement of its verb inside V′. Nominal arguments are DPs, with a silent D for each proper name. Finite I licenses nominative on its subject, and each transitive verb governs and assigns accusative to its object. The verbs are introduced as the inflected lexical forms liest and schreibt; abstract I bears matching present-tense and third-person singular features but is not a separately pronounced affix. Consequently, no morphological fusion or special token realization is required. The separate coordinator will eventually take the two completed CPs as its conjuncts.",
      "statement": "Construct two head-final German IPs and the coordinating head.",
