      "stageRecord": "Each verb adjoins to its own finite I before movement to C. This intermediate workspace makes the successive-cyclic head-movement commitment explicit: neither verb skips the intervening inflectional head. The lower V positions become silent head traces, while the inflected lexical terminals are pronounced in the newly formed complex I heads. Their lexical forms already agree with the finite features of I; this movement does not concatenate or respell morphological pieces. The objects remain in their original complement positions, and the subjects remain in Spec-IP. The argument and Case dependencies established in the preceding stage are preserved through the verbal chains.",
