      "stageRecord": "A head-initial C projection is built above each existing IP. Each complex finite I head moves to its local C, leaving an I trace, and each subject moves from its already established Spec-IP position to Spec-CP, leaving an A′-bound DP trace. These local operations produce one constituent before the finite verb in each conjunct: Mia before liest, and Leo before schreibt. Subject fronting here is a structural Vorfeld operation and does not require a contrastive-topic interpretation. The head chains proceed through V, I, and C without skipping a head; under the adopted GB treatment, the local head traces and subject traces meet the ECP. The subject chains retain the nominative Case and external theta roles licensed at their lower positions, and the objects retain accusative and their internal theta roles. The two completed CPs are then combined in an X-bar coordination projection: the first CP occupies Spec-&P, und heads &′, and the second CP is its complement. This is full clausal coordination, not gapping or shared-argument coordination; all movement is internal to a conjunct and creates no extraction from a coordinate island. The proper-name DPs are referential expressions and have no coindexed c-commanding antecedent, so Condition C is respected; there are no overt anaphors or pronouns requiring Conditions A or B. The completed structure is grammatical and yields exactly the supplied nine tokens, with no punctuation terminal because punctuation is absent from the token list.",
      "statement": "Complete both verb-second CPs and coordinate them into the grammatical surface sentence.",
